[ RVCD: READ A VARIABLE CONTROL DIAL THROUGH THE ARRAY.
[ THE MULTIPLEXER PUTS THE DIAL'S VOLTAGE BESIDE THE ARRAY'S X DATA
[ REGISTER, AND A COMPARATOR SETS SENSE LINE 24 WHEN X IS ABOVE IT
[ (SRM5 GHA4). WE FIND THE DIAL BY SUCCESSIVE APPROXIMATION: TRY EACH
[ BIT FROM THE TOP, AND KEEP IT IF X IS NOT YET ABOVE THE DIAL.
[ CALL:  JPSR RVCD; N     N = DIAL 0-5.  RETURN: AR = THE DIAL, A FRACTION.
CMP = 40                        [ SENSE LINE 24 IN THE LOWER HALF OF S4
RVCD:   0                       [ THE RETURN ADDRESS GOES HERE
        MDAR'I'X RVCD           [ THE DIAL'S NUMBER; STEP PAST IT
        ARMX                    [ SELECT IT ON THE MULTIPLEXER
        ARXO                    [ AR = 0
        ARMD RV.X
        ARXY                    [ COMPARE THE DIAL WITH 0
        SKLA CMP                [ 0 ABOVE THE DIAL: IT IS NEGATIVE
        JUMP RV.POS
        MDAR'F 1
        JUMP RV.GO
RV.POS: ARXO
RV.GO:  ARMD RV.NEG
        MDAR'F 20000            [ THE FIRST BIT TRIED: ONE HALF
        ARMD RV.B
RV.LP:  MDAR RV.X
        MDAE RV.B               [ TRY X + BIT
        ARMD RV.T
        MDAR RV.NEG
        JPLS RV.N1
        MDAR RV.T
        ARXY                    [ +T ABOVE THE DIAL?
        SKLA CMP
        JUMP RV.KEEP            [ NO: KEEP THE BIT
        JUMP RV.NEXT
RV.N1:  MDAR'N RV.T
        ARXY                    [ -T STILL ABOVE THE DIAL?
        SKLA CMP
        JUMP RV.NEXT            [ NO
RV.KEEP: MDAR RV.T
        ARMD RV.X
RV.NEXT: MDAR RV.B
        ARRS 1                  [ THE NEXT BIT DOWN
        ARMD RV.B
        JPLS RV.LP              [ UNTIL NO BITS ARE LEFT
        MDAR RV.NEG
        JPLS RV.MI
        MDAR RV.X
        JUMP'I RVCD
RV.MI:  MDAR'N RV.X
        JUMP'I RVCD
RV.X:   0
RV.B:   0
RV.T:   0
RV.NEG: 0
